# Day 38

**21km / 5.5 hours**

*Te Kuiti to Mangokewa North campsite*

A tricky day, mostly of my own making since I hung around in the town for a while. The day began slowly where I just dawdled and waited for the shops to open. When they were I bought an obscene amount of food from the supermarket to prepare for the upcoming days. I also voted in the NZ election! This all took a while but the primary reason for the delay was waiting for some other walkers to get into town so we could have lunch together and set off. The result of that was only getting going properly just before 2pm.

![The nice river I was walking past](./river.avif)

I naively thought it would be a gentle 20km or so for a nice afternoon but it was a tricky river walk featuring all the problems so far, i.e. mud, tricky navigation, technical sections, going up and down, heavy rain showers. 

![The footprint I left after my foot got stuck in there. It was up to my ankles which is a real pain](./mud-footprint.avif)

I got lost once and had to climb up the hillside to get to track that was passable, the problem was I was following the old track which had been left in disrepair and wasn't really usable since it featured very difficult climbing. It looked like the right way since it used to be so. This all added up to the track taking a lot longer than expected and being a lot tougher especially with the heavier than usual pack weighing on my shoulders.

Eventually I got to the campsite with a little daylight left which was a massive relief. Even if the weather was still playing with us it signalled the end of the walking.